prompt.text:
Implement a self-contained selection model using this exact API:

```ts
export interface Candidate {
  id: string;
  displayName: string;
}

export class CandidateList {
  constructor(candidates: readonly Candidate[], onPick: (id: string) => void);
  entries(): Candidate[];
  pick(id: string): boolean;
}
```

Each candidate ID and display name must be a non-empty string after trimming. Reject malformed candidates and duplicate IDs with `TypeError`; do not normalize accepted strings. The constructor must copy the array and its objects. `entries` returns fresh objects in original order, including candidates with duplicate display names.

`pick` searches by exact, case-sensitive ID. On a match it calls `onPick` once with that ID and returns true. For an unknown ID—including an empty string—it returns false without calling the callback. Candidate data must remain unchanged even if the caller later mutates the constructor input or an array returned by `entries`.

